# Leading and trailing underscores survive DSDL validation (only `_name_` is reserved) but the
# snake_case projection drops a leading one and keeps a trailing one, so `_foo` and `foo_` stay
# distinct by luck rather than by design.
# `_9axis` is legal too, and the projection drops the underscore that made it legal: a name
# beginning with a digit is an identifier in no target.
uint8 _foo
uint8 foo_
uint8 _9axis
uint8 bar
@sealed
